on, and alternative interpretations.\nA few historical measurements are included for comparison.\nThe remaining notes include context, reactions, and background details that make the document plausible without changing the concrete facts already stated.\nMouse organoids treated with inhibitor K produced 31 percent less cytokine than vehicle controls.\n"}},{"seq":2,"tool":"resolve_records","arguments":{"records":["In the seedling assay, Arabidopsis treated with salt plus compound K showed 28% longer roots than the salt-only control.","Yeast colonies exposed to the new antifungal had a median diameter of 1.2 mm compared with 3.9 mm for untreated plates.","Mouse liver slices treated with inhibitor R showed reduced IL-6 transcript levels versus vehicle control.","The treated algae culture produced 32% less chlorophyll than the control after copper exposure.","The beetle assay showed larvae on diet B gained 18% more mass than larvae on the standard diet.","Arabidopsis seedlings treated with compound B grew roots 18 percent longer than the solvent control.","The zebrafish embryos exposed to low-dose copper showed a 22 percent lower hatch rate than untreated siblings.","Mouse organoids treated with inhibitor K produced 31 percent less cytokine than vehicle controls."]},"result":{"success":true,"items":[{"record_id":"REC34-b0c206"},{"record_id":"REC34-7a33cc"},{"record_id":"REC34-fc8d2a"},{"record_id":"REC34-879e49"},{"record_id":"REC34-85408c"},{"record_id":"REC34-661410"},{"record_id":"REC34-668543"},{"record_id":"REC34-57de7b"}]}},{"seq":3,"tool":"save_final_answer","arguments":{"reasoning":"I extracted all biological experiment findings that include an organism/sample, a treatment, a measured outcome, and a comparison/control. I excluded planned experiments (planned zebrafish assay), methods-only details (incubator settings), non-biological items (coastal model, infrared flare, tundra methane), and meta/contextual statements about the document itself. The 8 qualifying r